      "model_answer": "In this context, the guest\u2019s statement\u2014**\"This soup could use a little something\"**\u2014is **not** being used in a literal sense about the soup itself. Instead, it is a **polite, indirect way of asking for a refill or more of the soup**.\n\n### **Literal Meaning (if taken literally):**\n- *\"The soup is missing something (e.g., seasoning, ingredients, or a garnish).\"*\n  *(This is unlikely in a social setting unless the soup is intentionally bland.)*\n\n### **True Intended Meaning (Polite Request):**\nThe speaker is **asking for more soup**\u2014likely because they are full or the portion was insufficient. The phrasing is a soft, non-confrontational way to say:\n- *\"Could you please pass me more soup?\"*\n- *\"I think I need another helping.\"*\n\n### **Why This Matters in Social Contexts:**\n- It avoids sounding demanding or rude.\n- It\u2019s a common way to politely request assistance in dining situations.\n- The speaker may also be subtly indicating they\u2019re satisfied with the soup but just need a little more.\n\nWould you like examples of how to respond appropriately?",
